  "document_coverage": "The source text explicitly describes the sequence of a spinal withdrawal reflex: painful stimulus activates sensory neurons, signals enter the spinal cord, interneurons excite flexor motor neurons and inhibit extensor motor neurons, creating a pattern that withdraws the limb. It notes that inhibition facilitates movement rather than stopping behavior entirely. It states the response begins before conscious awareness while ascending pathways carry info to the brain, and descending signals from the brain can modify spinal activity. The text concludes by framing this as local circuit processing within an interconnected nervous system.",
